# Digital Imaging and Conservation: Model Guidelines.

**Authors:** Dean, John F.

## Abstract
Examines the intersection of conservation and digital imaging based on guidelines at the Cornell University (Ithaca, NY) library. Discusses the digitization of artifacts; assessing the condition prior to scanning; scanning considerations, including temperature and humidity, lighting, and security; stable storage of artifacts after scanning; and grant-funded scanning project considerations. (LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ679606

